WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.280 --> 00:00:02.480
- Oh my gosh, this is
such a difficult question,

00:00:02.480 --> 00:00:03.400
because like...

00:00:04.280 --> 00:00:06.673
- Oh, I'm getting emotional. (laughs)

00:00:10.140 --> 00:00:11.473
Yeah, it's hard.

00:00:16.109 --> 00:00:19.100
(emotional music)

00:00:19.100 --> 00:00:22.790
I feel like loneliness
is really hard for me

00:00:22.790 --> 00:00:25.210
'cause I'm constantly
surrounded by people.

00:00:25.210 --> 00:00:28.730
But at the same time, when
I see people connecting

00:00:28.730 --> 00:00:29.850
and understanding each other,

00:00:29.850 --> 00:00:31.100
that's when I feel lonely.

00:00:31.100 --> 00:00:32.850
Is when I feel like I don't have anybody

00:00:32.850 --> 00:00:35.770
that understands me in that depth.

00:00:35.770 --> 00:00:37.600
Oh, I'm getting emotional. (laughs)

00:00:37.600 --> 00:00:38.900
But I feel like that's when I feel lonely,

00:00:38.900 --> 00:00:43.140
is when I see people
connecting on a deep level,

00:00:43.140 --> 00:00:44.510
when they don't have to say things.

00:00:44.510 --> 00:00:47.184
You just have that person
that understands you.

00:00:47.184 --> 00:00:48.017
- [Thoraya] You feel like you don't

00:00:48.017 --> 00:00:49.230
have anyone like that?
- Yeah, no I don't.

00:00:49.230 --> 00:00:51.940
And it sucks that I'm such a romantic,

00:00:51.940 --> 00:00:54.780
but I think loneliness for me,

00:00:54.780 --> 00:00:58.143
it comes from love, you know.

00:00:59.010 --> 00:01:02.170
Like loving somebody and
not having them there.

00:01:02.170 --> 00:01:03.690
Like that's so lonely.

00:01:03.690 --> 00:01:05.993
And knowing that they're
living their lives.

00:01:10.450 --> 00:01:11.343
Yeah, it's hard.

00:01:12.934 --> 00:01:14.646
(audio cuts) That guy.

00:01:14.646 --> 00:01:16.716
I'm just kidding, I'm just kidding.

00:01:16.716 --> 00:01:19.370
- When I was a child

00:01:19.370 --> 00:01:22.660
my mother was not able to
take care of our family

00:01:22.660 --> 00:01:27.480
and I was put into a
receiving home for children.

00:01:27.480 --> 00:01:29.720
So, probably then would probably be

00:01:30.582 --> 00:01:32.733
the ultimate one that sticks in my head.

00:01:33.671 --> 00:01:35.003
- [Thoraya] How old were you?

00:01:35.003 --> 00:01:37.263
- I was eight, eight years old.

00:01:38.120 --> 00:01:42.200
- I had a person in my life
who passed away very violently

00:01:42.200 --> 00:01:44.960
and I couldn't talk
about it for a long time.

00:01:44.960 --> 00:01:47.410
And that made me feel really lonely

00:01:47.410 --> 00:01:48.480
because there was a lot of shame

00:01:48.480 --> 00:01:49.980
and guilt that came with that.

00:01:51.570 --> 00:01:54.583
'Cause he killed himself
and somebody else.

00:01:56.276 --> 00:01:58.030
But the loneliness of that feeling

00:01:58.030 --> 00:02:02.957
and knowing that no one
else could understand

00:02:04.280 --> 00:02:07.943
was extremely isolating and
definitely really lonely.

00:02:09.370 --> 00:02:10.740
- The loneliest time I've ever been

00:02:10.740 --> 00:02:13.620
was when I had to live
in Saint Vincent de Paul

00:02:13.620 --> 00:02:16.630
over at 12th and Imperial,
pretty much for four years.

00:02:16.630 --> 00:02:17.820
And they're just homeless shelters

00:02:17.820 --> 00:02:21.240
for family and certain individuals

00:02:21.240 --> 00:02:23.310
and I lived there for about four years.

00:02:23.310 --> 00:02:25.490
- [Thoraya] So, you were
homeless for four years?

00:02:25.490 --> 00:02:29.050
- It's hard to explain how you don't feel

00:02:29.050 --> 00:02:31.110
like you're connected to the community.

00:02:31.110 --> 00:02:33.800
You're no longer part of
the whole world anymore.

00:02:33.800 --> 00:02:37.160
You feel so left out in that space.

00:02:37.160 --> 00:02:40.050
It's so much emptiness where you feel like

00:02:40.050 --> 00:02:42.400
even interacting with
people is really hard

00:02:42.400 --> 00:02:46.413
to even just say simple things like this.

00:02:47.890 --> 00:02:52.630
- Pretty much just always lonely.

00:02:52.630 --> 00:02:55.750
But not in a bad way, just keep to myself

00:02:55.750 --> 00:03:00.207
and always alone, but it's fine by me.

00:03:02.610 --> 00:03:04.560
- [Thoraya] So, you
kind of prefer your life

00:03:04.560 --> 00:03:06.280
to be that way, sounds like?

00:03:06.280 --> 00:03:10.000
- I mean it's like parallel
me wanting it to be that way

00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:11.383
and just how it falls.

00:03:13.550 --> 00:03:15.720
It just works out, I guess,

00:03:15.720 --> 00:03:17.283
or maybe I'm just used to it.

00:03:19.220 --> 00:03:20.940
- It's like which one do I pick?

00:03:20.940 --> 00:03:22.460
So, you know.

00:03:22.460 --> 00:03:25.320
I would say recent years,
the most loneliest time

00:03:25.320 --> 00:03:28.480
I felt was coming out to
my family as being bisexual

00:03:28.480 --> 00:03:31.600
and having that talk and
losing friends on the way.

00:03:31.600 --> 00:03:33.953
It's the whole, I went
through the whole phase of,

00:03:35.557 --> 00:03:37.360
"It's like an infection or something.

00:03:37.360 --> 00:03:39.320
Don't tell your little brother,

00:03:39.320 --> 00:03:41.260
he might turn out the
same way" kind of thing.

00:03:41.260 --> 00:03:44.330
So, it's like, "You know that's not true."

00:03:44.330 --> 00:03:48.270
It's like an old coming
out story in a sense.

00:03:48.270 --> 00:03:50.160
At least I'm not the 50 year old guy

00:03:50.160 --> 00:03:53.283
that's barely three divorces in.

00:03:54.126 --> 00:03:56.890
I finally feeling like I've
taken a hold of my life.

00:03:56.890 --> 00:03:58.940
You know, doing it now.

00:03:58.940 --> 00:04:00.750
- My husband died not too long ago,

00:04:00.750 --> 00:04:03.070
so I've never lived by myself.

00:04:03.070 --> 00:04:04.313
So, and it's lonely.

00:04:05.530 --> 00:04:07.760
Gonna be four years now.

00:04:07.760 --> 00:04:11.363
But it's still lonely.

00:04:12.440 --> 00:04:15.390
- [Thoraya] What's the
loneliest you've ever felt?

00:04:15.390 --> 00:04:16.736
- Oh, man.

00:04:16.736 --> 00:04:20.450
- I don't remember the
loneliest I've ever felt.

00:04:20.450 --> 00:04:22.300
- [Child] You could just say it.

00:04:22.300 --> 00:04:23.400
- Me getting divorced.

00:04:24.730 --> 00:04:26.510
That's the loneliest I've ever felt.

00:04:26.510 --> 00:04:27.895
- [Child] That is true.

00:04:27.895 --> 00:04:30.690
(everyone laughing)

00:04:30.690 --> 00:04:32.320
- Other than that, I don't
remember any other time.

00:04:32.320 --> 00:04:34.050
- [Thoraya] So, can you explain to us why

00:04:34.050 --> 00:04:35.450
that was such a lonely time?

00:04:38.090 --> 00:04:42.830
- I don't know, it just
felt empty that day.

00:04:42.830 --> 00:04:46.070
The day itself felt empty and weird,

00:04:46.070 --> 00:04:49.210
but that's probably the loneliest.

00:04:49.210 --> 00:04:51.873
I don't feel lonely ever since then.

00:04:53.070 --> 00:04:53.903
- [Thoraya] Is this your son?

00:04:53.903 --> 00:04:54.736
- My grandson.

00:04:54.736 --> 00:04:55.953
- [Thoraya] Your grandson.

00:04:58.201 --> 00:04:59.183
That's why what?

00:04:59.183 --> 00:05:01.713
- That's why I don't feel
lonely 'cause I have him.

00:05:03.670 --> 00:05:07.010
- When I was seven and
my mom went to rehab

00:05:08.320 --> 00:05:11.970
and so, that was like the first
time I really felt lonely.

00:05:11.970 --> 00:05:15.300
Because it was my first day of school

00:05:15.300 --> 00:05:18.380
and all the other parents
were with their kids

00:05:18.380 --> 00:05:20.485
taking them on their first day of school.

00:05:20.485 --> 00:05:21.320
And then I only have my dad

00:05:21.320 --> 00:05:23.370
and they all had their dads and moms, so.

00:05:25.940 --> 00:05:29.110
- At least like the
loneliest feeling to me

00:05:29.110 --> 00:05:32.920
would probably be the feeling,
not that no one's around

00:05:32.920 --> 00:05:36.840
but just no matter who you
try to explain something to,

00:05:36.840 --> 00:05:39.190
that nobody will understand
what you're saying.

00:05:41.040 --> 00:05:42.970
- When was the loneliest I've ever felt?

00:05:42.970 --> 00:05:45.480
Would probably be about two years ago

00:05:45.480 --> 00:05:47.060
when I lost someone really close to me.

00:05:47.060 --> 00:05:48.480
What happened?

00:05:48.480 --> 00:05:50.890
Pretty much, he was
going through a hard time

00:05:50.890 --> 00:05:53.350
and he did want me to be in a relationship

00:05:53.350 --> 00:05:56.250
that I did not want to
be in but I did it anyway

00:05:56.250 --> 00:05:58.190
and ended up losing all of my friends

00:05:58.190 --> 00:06:00.440
and he ended up killing himself

00:06:00.440 --> 00:06:05.440
and I stopped reaching out to people

00:06:05.590 --> 00:06:07.530
because nobody was all like...

00:06:07.530 --> 00:06:10.910
Everyone stopped being my
friend while I was with him.

00:06:10.910 --> 00:06:13.060
So, I didn't really
have anyone after that.

00:06:14.110 --> 00:06:14.943
Yeah.

00:06:14.943 --> 00:06:15.892
- [Thoraya] Did he commit suicide

00:06:15.892 --> 00:06:18.277
while you guys were in a
relationship together or after?

00:06:18.277 --> 00:06:20.253
- It was after I ended it.

00:06:22.340 --> 00:06:26.980
- The loneliest I've ever
felt was when I was 15

00:06:26.980 --> 00:06:31.010
and I was in high school and
I had literally no friends

00:06:31.010 --> 00:06:32.560
and people always made fun of me.

00:06:32.560 --> 00:06:34.610
That's probably the loneliness.

00:06:34.610 --> 00:06:37.400
- I usually just feel lonely
around the summertime.

00:06:37.400 --> 00:06:40.220
'Cause I'm not very good at
asking people to hang out

00:06:41.210 --> 00:06:42.700
especially during COVID time.

00:06:42.700 --> 00:06:45.070
'Cause I've just sort of
been staying on the computer,

00:06:45.070 --> 00:06:46.370
doing nothing.

00:06:46.370 --> 00:06:48.840
So, that's about the loneliness I feel.

00:06:48.840 --> 00:06:50.380
- That was definitely sophomore year

00:06:50.380 --> 00:06:52.540
when I was in high school,
I am in college now.

00:06:52.540 --> 00:06:54.340
So, I was always in class,

00:06:54.340 --> 00:06:57.610
always the last person to be
chosen on the table groups,

00:06:57.610 --> 00:06:59.600
always the last person to be chosen

00:06:59.600 --> 00:07:03.180
when there was any ever,
like a group project.

00:07:03.180 --> 00:07:04.013
And it was horrible.

00:07:04.013 --> 00:07:05.760
I use art as my coping mechanism.

00:07:05.760 --> 00:07:07.480
I would just be that sad kid in the corner

00:07:07.480 --> 00:07:09.090
drawing all my art projects

00:07:09.090 --> 00:07:10.657
and no one ever wanted to come up to me

00:07:10.657 --> 00:07:12.200
and I didn't want to go up to them

00:07:12.200 --> 00:07:14.760
because I just didn't feel
connected to any of them.

00:07:14.760 --> 00:07:17.540
If I could describe it in
one word, it would be lonely.

00:07:17.540 --> 00:07:21.720
- I grew up without a proper family.

00:07:21.720 --> 00:07:25.253
So, I've always felt lonely.

00:07:26.570 --> 00:07:28.720
I always feel like I'm
alone in everything.

00:07:32.110 --> 00:07:34.900
- I was pregnant with my last baby

00:07:34.900 --> 00:07:39.900
and I went through something
called antenatal depression.

00:07:41.410 --> 00:07:43.243
It was really lonely
where you just kind of...

00:07:43.243 --> 00:07:48.243
It's like postpartum, but
before the baby's born.

00:07:49.850 --> 00:07:51.993
So, it was really hard.

00:07:53.594 --> 00:07:55.960
I just feel alone and super sad

00:07:55.960 --> 00:07:57.830
and you just don't know why

00:07:57.830 --> 00:08:01.843
but it's really just your
hormones working against you.

00:08:03.710 --> 00:08:05.360
That was a really tough question.

00:08:06.261 --> 00:08:07.440
- [Thoraya] I'm so sorry.

00:08:07.440 --> 00:08:08.930
Is it okay that you're talking about it?

00:08:08.930 --> 00:08:09.763
Are you okay with that?

00:08:09.763 --> 00:08:10.900
- No, I'm fine.

00:08:10.900 --> 00:08:11.733
- [Thoraya] Do you feel better now

00:08:11.733 --> 00:08:13.380
or do you still feel it sometimes?

00:08:15.104 --> 00:08:20.104
- I think after kids,
everything always changes.

00:08:20.630 --> 00:08:24.540
Your body, your hormones,
everything is different.

00:08:24.540 --> 00:08:26.320
It does change you.

00:08:26.320 --> 00:08:30.550
So, I do still suffer with
depression and anxiety

00:08:31.610 --> 00:08:34.950
but I also have trauma from
my past and when I was a kid

00:08:34.950 --> 00:08:37.370
so that might not help.

00:08:37.370 --> 00:08:39.730
But that was like my loneliest time.

00:08:39.730 --> 00:08:42.400
Even though I had great
family, great support,

00:08:42.400 --> 00:08:47.020
I just still felt empty
and it was really sad

00:08:47.020 --> 00:08:51.760
because I was carrying a
life and I knew he felt it.

00:08:51.760 --> 00:08:56.693
So, it was like a really hard
and traumatizing experience.

00:08:56.693 --> 00:08:57.526
- [Thoraya] If someone's
going through it right now,

00:08:57.526 --> 00:09:00.313
what would you tell them to
help them get through it?

00:09:04.830 --> 00:09:08.003
- Take time to do things
that make you happy.

00:09:09.350 --> 00:09:14.033
It's so important. It's
okay to feel alone.

00:09:14.950 --> 00:09:18.110
But the point is to not just stay in that,

00:09:18.110 --> 00:09:19.713
you have to get out.

00:09:20.860 --> 00:09:24.830
Cry, talk to people that love you

00:09:25.820 --> 00:09:27.070
and just make sure you get up every day,

00:09:27.070 --> 00:09:28.480
get up every day, open your windows,

00:09:28.480 --> 00:09:30.380
open your windows bring in that light.

00:09:31.252 --> 00:09:33.760
Just give yourself more positive

00:09:33.760 --> 00:09:36.640
'cause it'll really drag you.

00:09:36.640 --> 00:09:39.280
People don't understand
pregnancy and women's hormones

00:09:39.280 --> 00:09:43.143
but you are not alone, we are all here.

00:09:45.270 --> 00:09:46.327
People see you.

00:09:47.450 --> 00:09:50.283
(emotional music)

00:09:51.210 --> 00:09:52.610
- Hey, everyone, before you go

00:09:52.610 --> 00:09:54.570
there's something I
want to share with you.

00:09:54.570 --> 00:09:56.990
So, you'll notice today
that there's a join button

00:09:56.990 --> 00:09:59.190
next to the subscribe button
on my YouTube channel.

00:09:59.190 --> 00:10:00.940
And I just wanted to explain to you

00:10:00.940 --> 00:10:02.820
why I decided to put that there.

00:10:02.820 --> 00:10:05.040
So, I have a pretty crazy dream

00:10:05.040 --> 00:10:07.190
where I'm hoping I can raise enough money

00:10:07.190 --> 00:10:09.170
to go all around the world and film

00:10:09.170 --> 00:10:11.010
in as many cities as possible,

00:10:11.010 --> 00:10:12.480
and as uncomfortable as I feel

00:10:12.480 --> 00:10:14.240
putting this join button on my channel,

00:10:14.240 --> 00:10:17.430
I think and I'm hoping
that maybe it's okay

00:10:17.430 --> 00:10:19.080
because one of the biggest requests

00:10:19.080 --> 00:10:22.430
from you all on my channel is
for me to film in new cities.

00:10:22.430 --> 00:10:23.760
So, now I'll explain to you all

00:10:23.760 --> 00:10:25.740
what the join button means exactly.

00:10:25.740 --> 00:10:27.080
When you go on my YouTube channel

00:10:27.080 --> 00:10:29.390
you'll notice that right
next to the subscribe button,

00:10:29.390 --> 00:10:30.690
there is a join button.

00:10:30.690 --> 00:10:33.410
Just to let you guys know,
the join button doesn't alter

00:10:33.410 --> 00:10:35.070
your subscription to my channel at all.

00:10:35.070 --> 00:10:37.020
You can still be subscribed to my channel

00:10:37.020 --> 00:10:38.440
and not join the membership.

00:10:38.440 --> 00:10:40.260
The join button is just
an additional thing

00:10:40.260 --> 00:10:41.410
if you choose to do it

00:10:41.410 --> 00:10:44.110
and if you don't do it,
that's totally fine, honestly.

00:10:44.110 --> 00:10:45.410
So, when you click the join button

00:10:45.410 --> 00:10:48.100
you'll see a page with three
different membership options

00:10:48.100 --> 00:10:49.100
that I've put together.

00:10:49.100 --> 00:10:51.420
And depending on which one
you choose to sign up for

00:10:51.420 --> 00:10:53.440
I offer you something in return.

00:10:53.440 --> 00:10:55.610
And if you do decide to sign up for one,

00:10:55.610 --> 00:10:58.270
honestly, thank you from
the bottom of my heart.

00:10:58.270 --> 00:11:00.880
And if you don't sign up for
one, that's totally fine too.

00:11:00.880 --> 00:11:03.000
You all do enough for me as it is.

00:11:03.000 --> 00:11:05.730
That's pretty much it. Thank
you guys for everything.

00:11:05.730 --> 00:11:08.253
I love you all and I'll see you next time.

